a grave) is Ulysses (Odysseus in Greek). When he was drafted for military
service to go to Troy, he rather stayed home with his wife and his newly
born kid.

Therefore, he pretended to be mad: he took two different animals (I
believe a mule and an ox) from the stables, put them in front of his
plough, and started ploughing the beach. Behind him, he sowed salt in the
newly made furrow, by throwing it over his left (!) shoulder.

